<!-- The Halo 3-style FRIENDS screen (the main menu's FRIENDS, Triangle in the lobbies) and the
FRIENDS panel at the right of the lobbies (port/linux/src/p2p_friends.h; menu_functions.c "port h3
friends ..."), laid out as Halo 3's friends list: the title strip with how many are online, this
Vita's friend code, ADD FRIEND, APPEAR OFFLINE and FRIENDS CAN JOIN, then the requests, invites,
friends (online first, what each is doing, JOIN when their game can be joined), the requests sent
and the blocked players, the chosen one's facts under the list, the buttons in the strip at the
foot. Cross does the row's first thing (Accept, Join, type a code), Square its second (Decline,
Invite, Ignore, Cancel), Triangle opens its options (Remove, Block, Unblock) after Halo 3's question.
The settings panel's Multiplayer > Friends does the same. The art is this folder's own
(tools/halo3_menu_art.py). -->
